  "limits": [
    "Four bounded 22-second native pan recordings; not a multi-hour endurance test. Tests use a disposable profile and the actual optimized Tauri/WebView2 app, standard memory/caches, and CDP mouse input. Instrumentation only observes native decode calls and governor decisions; it does not override their behavior.",
    "RAF and Cesium postRender cadence are not monitor presentation latency. Draw intervals follow requested input cadence and should not be read as a continuous FPS guarantee. Input timestamps and raw records remain under .qa/flight-pan-fix/native.",
    "The first streets/terrain pass retained one 148 ms UI task during initial tile loading. No UI task or RAF gap over 50 ms occurred in the warmed fast and slow streets passes or the no-map slow-input pass. This does not promise every possible loading pause is eliminated.",
    "CPU is normalized over 16 logical processors. RAM sums private resident memory over the app and child WebView processes. GPU load is attributed 3D engine utilization; GPU allocation is Windows process allocation accounting, not unique physical VRAM residency.",
    "Native rendered all 11,018 observations throughout; source IDs exactly matched engine output. The memory-pressure browser suite separately proves that real pressure still lowers framebuffer/geometry limits, preserves source records/selection/preferences, keeps playback available and recovers through all capped profiles.",
    "The source was first tested as an uncommitted tree and committed unchanged as the recorded feature commit. Source hashes match that commit; the follow-up commit contains validation records only.",
    "Release-update UI uses a fictional 0.16.13 response for the newly versioned app; this is not a published-release claim.",
    "No hosted runner, Public promotion, release/tag creation or installer execution. The updated local portable Windows executable is validated; existing running builds and user profiles were preserved."
  ]
